          "text": "Description: The witness observes twelve sparkling red-orange lights in the sky, moving randomly. The lights dim and eventually go out. Observing twelve sparkling red-orange lights in the sky, moving randomly, on a Saturday night into Sunday, especially in August in a tourist area, suggests Thai lanterns, often released after festivals. Meteociel indicates a light south wind and cloudy weather for that evening. The information provided by the witness (unspecified observation and movement direction) does not allow this movement to be compared with local wind to confirm this hypothesis. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", unremarkable, probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
